  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We've recently been given the PlayHapticEventInHand Udon node, and the HapticEvent have already existed for a while in SDK2, but since an update quite a while ago (about a year?) the haptics are honestly too weak to bother using. The haptics can be heard, but not felt properly. This is at the case for at least Vive and rift S. I tried messing with the parameter values for the haptic event using UdonSharp, but I didn't succeed in achieving proper strength.\n\nEdit: I found additional information in the comments of a similar post, it might explain the missing haptic power:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-feedback/p/expose-vrcplayerapiplayhapticeventinhand-for-udon\n\nAn implimentation of the haptic event, which had proper strength in the past, can be found in the \"Collar and lead\" world. I get that strong Haptics will drain the battery faster, but I really want this feature (or is it a bug fix in this case?) and it's probably not much work to implement.",
